<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 1.6 pct in May - Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 1.6 pct in May - Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	     May 97  April 97	 May 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.3	  0.1	  0.4</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     1.6	  1.7	  4.3</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    105.7	105.4	104.0</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 1.6 percent year-on-year in May.  </p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     104.1	   0.0	   -0.6</p>
<p> Clothing			 106.7	  +0.1	   +2.6</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   109.4	   0.0	   +4.0</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 105.4	  +0.3	   +1.5</p>
<p> Health spending		105.7	  +0.1	   +2.9</p>
<p> Transport			106.2	  +0.3	   +1.5</p>
<p> Recreation		     103.4	   0.0	   +0.5</p>
<p> Education			107.5	  +0.1	   +3.5</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  106.4	  +0.3	   +2.4</p>
<p> Other goods,service	  105.1	  +1.4	   +2.0</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
